  "label": "Military General",
  "description": "A high-ranking officer in the armed forces, typically commanding a large unit or responsible for strategic operations. In this meme, the general is depicted as a figure of authority and lethal force, representing state-sanctioned violence. The specific general in the image is General Mark Milley, the former Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the United States, though his identity is not necessary to understand the meme’s structure — the concept of a military general as a symbol of state violence is sufficient.",
